# ============================================================
# SECTION 1: IMPORTS AND SHARED SETTINGS
# ============================================================
#
# - Import the libraries needed for the project.
# - Define the start codons and stop codons.
# - Agree on the format used to store each ORF.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 2: DNA INPUT AND VALIDATION
# ============================================================
#
# Function: load_dna()
# - Read a DNA sequence from a file.
# - Remove unnecessary whitespace and convert to uppercase.
# - Return the cleaned DNA sequence.
#
# Function: validate_dna()
# - Check that the DNA sequence contains valid DNA characters.
# - Decide how to handle unknown bases such as N.
# - Return whether the sequence is valid.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 3: REVERSE COMPLEMENT
# ============================================================
#
# Function: reverse_complement()
# - Replace each DNA base with its complementary base.
# - Reverse the resulting sequence.
# - Return the reverse-complement sequence.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 4: FIND ORFs IN ONE READING FRAME
# ============================================================
#
# Function: find_orfs_in_frame()
# - Scan a DNA sequence in one reading frame.
# - Identify start codons and stop codons.
# - Record candidate ORFs and their coordinates.
# - Store details such as strand, frame and length.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 5: SEARCH ALL SIX READING FRAMES
# ============================================================
#
# Function: find_orfs()
# - Search all three reading frames on the forward strand.
# - Search all three reading frames on the reverse strand.
# - Combine the results into one list of ORFs.
# - Assign each ORF a unique ID.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 6: FILTER ORFs
# ============================================================
#
# Function: filter_orfs()
# - Filter ORFs by minimum and maximum length.
# - Allow filtering by strand.
# - Allow filtering by reading frame.
# - Return the filtered ORFs.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 7: CALCULATE STATISTICS
# ============================================================
#
# Function: calculate_statistics()
# - Calculate the total number of ORFs.
# - Calculate the shortest, longest and average ORF lengths.
# - Count codons and amino acids.
# - Return the statistics in an organised format.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 8: EXPORT RESULTS
# ============================================================
#
# Function: export_results()
# - Save ORF information to a CSV file.
# - Include IDs, coordinates, strand, frame and length.
# - Include the DNA sequence for each ORF.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 9: MAIN PROGRAM
# ============================================================
#
# Function: main()
# - Load and validate the DNA sequence.
# - Find ORFs across all six reading frames.
# - Filter the ORFs if required.
# - Calculate statistics.
# - Export the results.
# - Display a summary to the user.
#
# ============================================================
# SECTION 10: TESTING
# ============================================================
#
# - Test with a short DNA sequence where the expected ORFs
#   are known.
# - Test invalid DNA input.
# - Test sequences with no ORFs.
# - Test both forward and reverse strands.
# - Check that coordinates and lengths are correct.
#
